# C8 anion addition: FREE HOO- reference (bare anion, no counter-ion).
#
# Binding-energy reference for cat + HOO- -> [cat...HOO-]- (Rs = rs_anion).
# BARE anion on BOTH sides: the counter-cation is deliberately excluded so the
# reaction balances on the anion (cat is neutral). Carrying a counter-ion onto
# only this reference would make the reaction cat + [M+ HOO-] -> [cat...HOO-]- +
# M+, which is not the intrinsic cat<->HOO- binding. A cation is a diagnostic
# only if charged-species solvation looks pathological.
#
# Geometry = atoms {130,131,132} of rs_anion/job.xyz (the HOO- fragment). It is
# relaxed here, so the perturbed input geometry is only a seed.
#
# Isolated species: no host, no QM/MM. Isolated-species convention is
# CPCM(Water) (the geometry tier of the complex uses ddCOSMO only because plain
# CPCM is not implemented for QM/XTB). B97-3c. Opt + Freq in ONE job.
! B97-3c CPCM(Water) Opt Freq TightOpt TightSCF

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile -1 1 job.xyz
